<Layout title="How to play a ROM hack or translation | Legacy of Goku Hub" description="How to apply a Legacy of Goku ROM hack or translation patch to your own copy of the game."><main id="main" class="container prose"><h1>How to play a ROM hack or translation</h1><p>ROM hacks and translations are shared as patch files. A patch holds only the changes, so you supply the original game yourself. The Hub does not host or link to ROMs.</p><ol><li>Start from your own cartridge. Copy the game you own to a .gba file with a cartridge reader.</li><li>Check which version the patch needs. The project's own page or readme names the region and revision it was built on, often with a checksum. A patch applied to a different version usually gives a broken game.</li><li>Apply the patch. Patch files end in .ips, .ups or .bps. Open <a href="https://www.marcrobledo.com/RomPatcher.js/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Rom Patcher JS</a> in your browser, choose your .gba file and the patch file, and save the patched copy.</li><li>Play the patched file in a Game Boy Advance emulator such as <a href="https://mgba.io/" rel="noopener noreferrer">mGBA</a>, or on a flash cartridge. Keep the original file unchanged so you can patch it again when the project updates.</li></ol><p>Fan games and tools are separate downloads and need no patch. Stuck? Ask in the <a href={discordURL} rel="noopener noreferrer">Discord</a> or on the project's own page.</p></main></Layout>
